          <attvalue for="33" value="-" />
          <attvalue for="29" value="2" />
          <attvalue for="35" value="0.6" />
          <attvalue for="36" value="An abrupt increase in global short-term policy rates raises near‑term borrowing costs and recession risk, prompting governments to defer politically and fiscally costly integration measures (new pooled funds, membership expansions) and thereby lowering institutional integration pressure." />
